nearly seven months after the assault on  the capitol washington dc's metropolitan  police say  two more police officers who responded  to the riot  recently died by suicide that raises the  total  of known police suicides to four since  the attack  by supporters of president trump chris  van cleeve is on capitol hill this  morning looking at the impact of those  who defended the capital  on january 6. chris good morning david  good morning it is just heartbreaking  think back one week ago  we were watching as officers battled  back their emotions as they provided  harrowing testimony about their  terrifying experiences  during the attack on the capitol on  january 6th now we're learning the d.c  police department is mourning the loss  of two of their own  an 18-year veteran and a five-year  veteran both  lost to suicide officer gunther hashida  was found dead at his home according to  d.c police on thursday  he was assigned to the emergency  response team and according to his  obituary the father of three  died just shy of his 44th birthday  officer  kyle defrytag was found dead in july d.c  police say he was just  26 years old there are now four known  suicides by officers who responded to  the assault on the capitol  i recently spoke with dc police officer  michael fanon about the impacts of the  insurrection  on him how is it affecting you now there  was a time where i dealt with  some severe and i still experienced like  severe depression  you know almost debilitating like early  on i mean i had like bouts of just like  absolute  like rage i think that was like the  overwhelming  emotion that i experienced like pretty  early on or just like  unbelievable sadness  almost unexplained at the time you know  the justice department has charged more  than 550 people  in relation to the attack on the capitol  on january 6th  and the house select committee is  continuing its investigation  into what happened gail all right thank  you very much chris
 

